\f0\fs24 \cf0 \
Every context already publishes domain events for integration. The remaining question is whether a context's own source of truth is the current state (state-oriented / CRUD) or the full append-only event log (event-sourced), with current state and every read model rebuilt from it.\
\
We apply event sourcing selectively: to the four contexts where an audit trail, incident reconstruction, or retroactive AI feature extraction has real business value \'97 Ticketing & Passes, Ride Telemetry & Safety, Animal Welfare Telemetry, and Visitor Insight & Personalization. Identity & Visitor Accounts and Payments stay state-oriented \'97 they're generic, solved-problem subdomains where an event store buys complexity without buying much.\
Fig 5,6,7\
An append-only log and a visitor's right to be forgotten are in tension. Ticketing events will carry personal data \'97 see the AI Feedback watch points below, and forthcoming ADR-8.\
\
Considered Options\
\
Two separate axes: A-C decide how the platform splits into contexts; D-F decide how those contexts keep their own state.\
A. Single monolithic \'93Estate Platform\'94 with one shared data model \'97 rejected: couples safety-critical ride data to marketing personalization, and blocks independent iteration on Visitor Insight without redeploying ticketing.\
B. Six bounded contexts, event-integrated \'97 CHOSEN. Matches the three domains named in the brief, isolates the safety-critical ride path from analytics, and lets the AI-heavy core domain evolve independently.\
C. Two contexts only, Commerce vs Telemetry \'97 rejected: still conflates ride safety with animal welfare (different cadence and criticality) and conflates ticketing with AI personalization (different rate of change).\
D. State-oriented (CRUD) persistence everywhere \'97 rejected as the sole approach: throws away the audit trail and replay capability that Ride Telemetry, Animal Welfare, Ticketing and Visitor Insight would all benefit from.\
E. Event sourcing for every context, uniformly \'97 rejected: forces an event store, snapshotting and projection-rebuild machinery onto Identity and Payments, where nothing about the problem calls for it.\
F. Event sourcing where it earns its keep \'97 CHOSEN. Event-sourced for Ticketing & Passes, Ride Telemetry & Safety, Animal Welfare Telemetry and Visitor Insight & Personalization; state-oriented for Identity and Payments.\
