\f1\b \cf0 Consequences & Trade-offs\
\pard\tx0\tx0\tx567\tx1134\tx1701\sl312\slmult1\pardirnatural\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 Positive\
Safety-critical ride telemetry is isolated from experimental AI/personalization code \'97 a bad model in Visitor Insight can't block gate entry or an e-stop signal.\
The core domain can iterate quickly and stay AI-heavy, decoupled from the more conservatively-changing supporting contexts.\
Matches the three domains already named in the brief, so it should translate cleanly into team and AI-assisted ownership.\
Event sourcing on Ticketing, Ride Telemetry, Animal Welfare and Visitor Insight gives a full audit trail, safety-incident reconstruction, and the ability to backfill new AI metrics from history instead of re-instrumenting the park.\
Negative\
Six contexts means six things to deploy, monitor and secure instead of one \'97 real overhead a kata-scale build must account for (ADR-3).\
The Ticketing<->Identity Shared Kernel is a known coupling risk without a named owner.\
The six-way map needs discipline, or Visitor Insight will end up reaching directly into another context's database as a shortcut.\
Event-sourced contexts need snapshotting once their logs grow, and a schema-evolution (upcasting) strategy for event payloads over the estate's lifetime.\
An immutable event log makes deleting one visitor's personal data harder.\
AI Feedback (per ADR-0)\
The Shared Kernel between Ticketing & Passes and Identity & Visitor Accounts is the riskiest relationship on this map. Name a single owner for it now, before it calcifies.\
\'93Safety-critical\'94 for Ride Telemetry & Safety is asserted here but not yet backed by a concrete latency/availability target \'97 ADR-6 should quantify that so this isolation is testable, not aspirational.\
Collapsing every AI use case into one Visitor Insight context is a reasonable v1 simplification, but an animal-health anomaly detector and a marketing recommendation carry very different risk profiles in reality. Flag as a candidate future split, not settled.\
Open question for the Countess/stakeholder: is Payments truly generic, or does family-pass pricing/discounting belong closer to Ticketing than to a generic payment gateway? Worth confirming before ADR-5.\
Event sourcing on Ticketing & Passes means the log will contain personal data tied to an identifiable visitor. An append-only store and a GDPR erasure request are in direct tension \'97 resolve with crypto-shredding (encrypt per-visitor, delete the key) or by keeping personal data out of the event payload and referencing it by pseudonymous ID instead. Treat as a hard requirement for ADR-8, not an afterthought.\
Snapshotting policy for Ride Telemetry & Safety and Animal Welfare Telemetry isn't decided here \'97 with 40 rides and 55 enclosures streaming continuously, replaying from event zero stops being cheap well before year three's 15,000-visitor target.\
